        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "cbd69f9e-a4b3-5703-96d2-43371a7cae2d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Inter-Allied Socialist Conferences of World War I, First World War, 1900 Hoboken Docks Fire\n- Organizations: socialist parties of the Entente or Allied powers\n- Places: Bremen, Baltimore\n- Products: SS Main\n- Concepts: Allies of World War I, Entente Powers, Central Powers\n\nFacts:\n- During the First World War, there were several Inter-Allied Socialist Conferences involving the socialist parties of the Entente or Allied powers.\n- The Allies of World War I, also called the Entente Powers, were the countries that opposed the Central Powers in the First World War.\n- SS Main was launched in 1900 and served on the route from Bremen to Baltimore.\n- SS Main was involved in the 1900 Hoboken Docks Fire.\n- SS Main remained on the Bremen to Baltimore route until the Allies of World War I seized her in 1914.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
